Gonna disagree with the last author ...

... some of the older spoiler files recommend using the iron ball as a
weapon, as it is not bad at all in the early game.  It's heavy and does
a lot of damage.

So yes, this idea has been thought of before and at least some players
have found it good.

The downside, of course, is that A) it's heavy and B) there are a
number of ways to get killed by your own iron ball.  These risks can be
mitigated but not entirely avoided with some common sense.

My suggestion:  by all means use it if you get stuck with it,  but
don't seek it out.

Getting rid of the ball and chain ... I want to keep this spoiler free,
so I won't tell you outright ... but AFAIK it is virtually impossible
for *you* to remove it by *conventional* means.     Whether someone
else could do it, or whether there are unconventional methods that
would work,  I leave for you to discover.

Above comments are, I believe, 100% spoiler-free. Will provide spoilers
if you desire. 

